.TH MEMCPY 3 2026-02-06 "Substrate LibC" "Substrate Library Functions"
.SH NAME
memcpy \- copy memory area
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <string.h>
.sp
.BI "void *memcpy(void *" dest ", const void *" src ", size_t " n ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.BR memcpy ()
function copies
.I n
bytes from memory area
.I src
to memory area
.IR dest .
The memory areas must not overlap. Use
.BR memmove (3)
if the memory areas do overlap.
.SS Implementation Notes
This implementation is optimized using word-aligned transfers on 32-bit boundaries.
Small copies (< 4 bytes) use byte-by-byte copying.
Larger transfers align to 4-byte boundaries and copy 32-bit words for approximately
3-4x speedup compared to naive byte-by-byte implementations.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The
.BR memcpy ()
function returns a pointer to
.IR dest .
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
#include <string.h>
#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
    char src[] = "Hello";
    char dest[6];
    memcpy(dest, src, 6);
    printf("%s\\n", dest);
    return 0;
}
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR memmove (3),
.BR memset (3),
.BR strcpy (3)
